{"join() timeout handling breaks outer loop if remaining_time <= 0, skipping termination of remaining processes": 0.8731733560562134, "SpanFlusher discards the SpansBuffer instance shared with RunTask and creates new per-process buffers, so the producer writes to one buffer while workers flush different buffer instances, breaking data flow and leaving written spans unflushed": 0.6759076714515686, "Race condition where multiple processes can flush the same segment if Redis writes race - if a segment is in the queue but hasn't been deleted yet, another process's next flush cycle could pick it up before the first process calls done_flush_segments()": 0.20310334861278534, "submit() assumes buffers dict is populated but if there is any exception during buffer initialization or process creation in __init__, self.buffers could be partially populated or empty, causing silent operation on incomplete set of buffers": 0.14162097871303558, "When a process restarts and _create_process_for_shards() is called again, the old buffer reference in self.buffers[process_index] is overwritten without proper cleanup, causing silent data loss, inconsistent metrics, and missed backpressure signals": 0.4101119637489319, "join() calls terminate() on processes still alive after deadline but doesn't verify termination succeeded": 0.29972752928733826}